-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Underwurlde
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1984
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Underwurlde (1984)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         9a031797ed0cc96a9ec286ed22a32317

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every moving figure:
              Sabreman with fair hair and skin, brown winged beasts shaded
              grey, pale-blue jellyfish, orange flying bugs, bubbles, weapons
              and items in their own colours; rooms, furniture, the rope and
              the panel unchanged. No white outlines or edges. The palette is
              fitted to the figures so Sabreman's eyes stay apart from his
              skin. Source: Enhanced colours: the Spec256 team, from their
              Spec256 conversion of the game.

  Pace        original (-0.08% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe 38183
              with IX 36634 (the player's own update); 3 trials per scene from
              the same RAM, each at its own video phase; single trials -0.66
              to +0.91%; player position and room equal to the original at
              every update)

  Changes     1.0: review build, not published: figures as Next sprites, the
              Spec256 conversion's colours as Enhanced.
              1.1: Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11
              safe); the game's speed restored after every hook; R kept as the
              original's; original pace; the game's own interrupt routine at
              its own clock; the approved Enhanced colours unchanged; the
              tape's loading screen; five checked trainers

  Note        Keys: on the game's selection screen 1 keyboard, 2 Kempston, 3
              cursor or 4 Interface II, then 0 to start; on the keyboard Q, W,
              E and R move and T fires. Every moving figure (Sabreman, the
              creatures, weapons and items) is a Next sprite in the game's own
              colours; plants, stalactites, furniture, the rope, the panel and
              text stay as the original draws them. The original 48K game with
              its beeper sound. Known issues: a figure past the far right edge
              (X over 232) is cut off at the edge, where the original wraps
              its pixels onto the next screen row; not seen in testing.
              Missing: not reached in testing: natural play to the end (the
              deep rooms and the ending reached from labelled cheat and
              teleport starts only), joysticks; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite gems
   3  No enemies
   4  Weapons stay put
   5  Start with 9 lives

  The archive's POKEs for this release, translated to the game's loading
  address. Weapons stay put corrected: the archive's address leaves four
  weapon layouts, the corrected one gives one.

